## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: Câu hỏi phỏng vấn

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

2 phút podcast. Nghe → dừng → nhại to.

### 16:40–16:55 · Trả lời có ghi âm

**Câu hỏi tuần này:** *"Where do you store auth tokens in a mobile app, and why?"*

> *"Access tokens and refresh tokens go in SecureStore, which maps to the Keychain on iOS and the Keystore on Android. They're encrypted at the OS level, so even on a rooted device they're much harder to pull out than a plain file.*
> *I don't use AsyncStorage for anything sensitive. It's just a file inside the app sandbox — no encryption at all. It's fine for cache and user preferences, not for credentials.*
> *One practical gotcha is that SecureStore has a size limit of about two kilobytes per key on iOS, and a JWT with a refresh token can exceed that. So you either chunk the value across keys or store only the refresh token securely.*
> *And I'd say the bigger point is that client-side storage is only one layer. Short token lifetimes and proper checks on the server matter more — if someone gets a token off a device, the real protection is that it expires quickly."*

**Ba nhịp:** *claim → evidence → boundary*. Câu cuối là boundary, và nó là câu khiến người phỏng vấn nâng đánh giá của bạn lên.

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `at rest` | dữ liệu lúc lưu trữ | *Encrypted at rest.* |
| `gotcha` (n) | cái bẫy nhỏ hay dính | *One practical gotcha is…* |
| `chunk` (v) | chia nhỏ ra | *You chunk the value across keys.* |
| `pull out` | lấy ra, trích ra | *Hard to pull out of the Keychain.* |
| `short-lived` (adj) | có thời hạn ngắn | *Access tokens are short-lived.* |

